You'll get plenty of responsibility, but you won’t be on your own: Rik, our copy and content specialist will guide you, with regular check-ins to support your growth. Depending on your interests, you might also design visuals for social media and the website, gather stories and content from colleagues and clients, analyse LinkedIn performance, look for backlinking opportunities, or conduct market and competitor research. You'll join all team marketing meetings, giving you insight into how a fast-growing scale-up builds its brand.
 Why go Greener? 
Besides contributing to a greener world, here's what you'll get:
 Exciting and important work in a rapidly growing scale-up;
 An inspiring work environment with a committed, friendly team and an open and honest work culture;
 A monthly internship allowance of € 400 gross;
 Travel reimbursement if you don't have access to free public transport;
 Free vegetarian lunch at our Amsterdam office;
 A laptop of your choice to use for the duration of your internship (Apple or Microsoft);
 Who are you? 
You’re someone who likes to take initiative, enjoys variety in your day, and thrives in a fast-moving environment. You don’t need to know everything yet, it's more important that you enjoy figuring things out, asking questions, and improving your skills. Besides that, you (are):
 A true Greener – you want to make the world a bit better, you question the status quo, and you're always looking for ways to innovate and improve;
 Fluent in Dutch and English (fluency in French, Spanish, or German is a big plus)
 Studying communications/media/marketing in an educational institution in the Netherlands (HBO/WO)
 Enjoy learning by doing and have a hands-on mindset;
 Are organised, and not afraid to speak up or try new things.
 Experience with tools like LinkedIn, WordPress, HubSpot, or Canva is a nice bonus, but don't worry if you're new to them, we'll help you figure it out! 
 Who are we? 
We are Greener Power Solutions, officially a Great Place to Work® (yes, we’ve got the certificate to prove it!). We’re on a mission to make the temporary energy market emission-free with our mobile batteries. These can be deployed anywhere to store and deliver energy. It’s an important mission, and we could really use your help.
 At Greener, we're not only committed to a greener world but also to a fair, inclusive, and diverse work environment. Different perspectives and experiences drive innovation and sustainability. We encourage people from all backgrounds to apply. 
Do you see yourself as our marketing intern? Apply now with your CV and a brief motivation, and Rik will get in touch with you within 5 working days!

